Modification Notice
===================

This APK (ADBKeyBoard.apk) is a modified build of senzhk/ADBKeyBoard
(https://github.com/senzhk/ADBKeyBoard), an Android input method (IME) that
accepts text input via ADB broadcasts.

Modification: Deep-link input support
--------------------------------------
In addition to the original broadcast-based input mechanism, this modified
version adds support for receiving text input through a deep link (intent)
of the form:

    adbkeyboard://input?b64=<base64-encoded-text>

This allows automation frameworks (such as Maestro's `openLink` command) to
inject text into the active input field via an ADB deep-link intent, without
relying solely on the broadcast mechanism.

The deep-link path decodes the base64 payload from the query string and
forwards it to the same AdbIME text-input handler used by the original
broadcast flow.

All modifications are released under the same GPLv2 license as the original
project.
